# Skills Editorial SoT

**Role:** present-tense procedures for this scanner + pointers to living docs and rules. **Not:** policy SoT, living-doc template library, or generic agent-framework tutorial.

Ownership: [DOC-OWNERSHIP.md](../../.specs/codebase/DOC-OWNERSHIP.md). Inventory: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md). Lint: `lintSkillsDoc` in [`living-sot-doc.mjs`](../hooks/lib/living-sot-doc.mjs) (regex subset: foreign requirement IDs, gate tiers, nonexistent tooling, web-app examples) — prose rules below stay manual review.

## Forbidden

- Generic web-app examples — React / `.tsx`, auth flows, `Database` as a SoT. This package is a Node CLI (git churn + NCLOC + scoring)
- Gate tiers (`quick` / `full` / `build`) — the single required gate is [quality-gates.mdc](quality-gates.mdc)
- Requirement ID prefixes other than `HOTSPOT-*` — see [feature-planning.mdc](feature-planning.mdc)
- Full living-doc templates — destinations live in DOC-OWNERSHIP, editorial rules in the matching `*-sot.mdc`
- References to nonexistent tooling (Context7, mermaid-studio, …) — cite only commands and files that exist in this repo

## Allowed

- Present-tense procedures, phase steps, checklists, `Do NOT use for …` anti-triggers
- Short pointers to living docs, `*-sot.mdc` rules, agents under `.cursor/agents/`, and `docs/cli-reference.md`

## Sync

Update when a procedure changes. Policy text stays in its own SoT; milestone-dependent prose → ROADMAP / STATE / feature specs.
